{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update-26.json\",\"summary\":\"Recording the outcome of the last unexercised combination with its concrete reason rather than leaving it unmentioned. Restarting members inside the randomized exploration was attempted locally and abandoned: that harness drives the state machines directly and never appends the unstable log or hard state to storage, so a restart there reloads an empty log and models storage loss rather than recovery. The attempt made that explicit, with the restarted instance's committed index resetting to zero and the instance panicking with tocommit out of range for a log of last index 0 and once with need non-empty snapshot, which is the target reacting to a lost log while the hard state claims committed entries, not a defect witness. The harness was reverted to its verified revision and its exploration test passes again. The exploration interpretation is revised to add that limitation with this reason and to point at the separate recovery scenario on the Node API, whose driver does persist hard state and entries on every Ready and where the restarted member fetched the missed entry, relearned the leader and proposed successfully. The submission carries no experiment and requests no execution; the audit's remaining records now state, per question, what is witnessed, what is bounded and what was deliberately not sampled.\"}"}}
